==Early entrants==
===College underclassmen===
For the fourth year in a row and the eighth time in nine years, no college underclassman would withdraw their entry into the NBA draft. However, it would be the first time in NBA history that a player that qualified for the status of a "college underclassman" would be playing professional basketball overseas, as [[Cedric Henderson (basketball, born 1965)|Cedric Henderson]] (who had previously played for the [[Georgia Bulldogs men's basketball|University of Georgia]] for a year before travelling to [[Italy]] to play for the [[Olimpia Milano|Simac Olimpia Milano]]) would qualify as an official entry there, expanding the list of official players there from eight to nine. Excluding him, however, the following [[college basketball]] players successfully applied for early draft entrance.<ref>{{cite web |title=1986 Underclassmen |url=https://www.thedraftreview.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=3033:1986-underclassmen&catid=136&Itemid=384 |website=The Draft Review | date=August 4, 2007 |access-date=October 23, 2024}}</ref>

{{div col}}
